From 1bc068af0aa2e0c0aea3694552774022e7e02729 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 23:40:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix setRootNode() assertion when the outgroup is absent from
 a partition tree or a quartet tree

With -o, PhyloTree::setRootNode() is also called on the per-partition trees
of a supertree (saveCheckpoint()/getTreeString() during the fast ML tree
search, PartitionModel::computeMarginalLhForPartitions()) and on the
4-taxon quartet trees of likelihood mapping. A partition tree does not
contain a taxon that has no data in that partition and a quartet tree
contains only its four taxa, so findNodeName() returned null and
ASSERT(root) aborted with

  phylotree.cpp:486: PhyloTree::setRootNode(): Assertion `root' failed.

Skip outgroup taxa that are not in the tree at hand and, if none is left,
root the tree at its first taxon as when no outgroup is given. The outgroup
is still validated against the alignment elsewhere, so a misspelled -o
still stops with an error. Runs without -o, and runs where the outgroup has
data in every partition, are unchanged.

Add two commands on the turtle data (phrynops has no data in the fourth
partition) to test_iqtree.sh/.ps1 and their log-likelihoods to
expect_ans.txt.

Fixes #203, fixes #89.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TaHntBDKuZJpMAAMenkC44
---
 test_scripts/test_data/expect_ans.txt |  2 ++
 test_scripts/test_iqtree.ps1          |  4 +++
 test_scripts/test_iqtree.sh           |  6 +++++
 tree/phylotree.cpp                    | 36 +++++++++++++++++----------
 4 files changed, 35 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

